                <pb facs="0435" n="347" sameAs="frus:frus1933v04/pg347"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">724.3415/3244: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Brazil</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Thurston</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Rio de
                                Janerio</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1933-07-25T17:00:00-03:00">July 25, 1933—5
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received July 25—4:15 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>69. Embassy’s 58, May 31, 2 p.m. I have just been informed at the Foreign Office
                    that a public statement will be issued tonight announcing that arrangements with
                    the League of Nations and Bolivia and Paraguay have been made whereunder the
                    ABCP states will undertake to effect a settlement of the Chaco conflict.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Thurston</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
